    These are Obel MS's own prices. See the full <a href="/pricing">pricing page</a>
    for a feature-by-feature breakdown of each plan, plus add-ons for extra users, storage and AI usage.
  </p>

  <h2>What should you ask a vendor before you sign?</h2>
  <p>
    A short checklist catches most of the surprises. Send this list to any vendor you're evaluating and ask
    for written answers before you compare their number to anyone else's.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Is the headline price per user, per company, or tiered? What happens as our team grows?</li>
    <li>Does the price include implementation, validation and training, or are those separate projects?</li>
    <li>Is there a setup or onboarding fee, and is it once-off or recurring?</li>
    <li>What support is included, and what response time can we expect in writing?</li>
    <li>Where is our data hosted, and who can access it?</li>
    <li>Can we get a full export of our documents, metadata and audit trail if we leave?</li>
    <li>Is the quote VAT-inclusive, and in what currency will we be billed?</li>
    <li>Is there a minimum contract term, and what's the cost of leaving early?</li>
    <li>Are there limits on storage, users or automated processing, and what do overages cost?</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Write the answers down next to each vendor's headline price. Once implementation, VAT, currency and
    contract length are accounted for, the real gap between a cheap self-serve tool and a mid-tier hosted
    system is usually smaller than the sticker price suggests. The gap to an enterprise eQMS platform is
    usually larger.
  </p>
